        "original_id": "83a1927d-dd1c-5f6e-8599-2783c972c4d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: A Christmas Carol (1938 film), Gulliver's Travels (1939)\n- People: Charles Dickens, Reginald Owen\n- Topics: Afternoon movie television programming, Christmas season broadcasts, Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade\n\nFacts:\n- In the Christmas season, local television stations sometimes telecast afternoon films after the network broadcast of the Macy's Thanksgiving Day Parade.\n- In those Christmas-season broadcasts, local stations sometimes showed Gulliver's Travels (1939) and A Christmas Carol (1938).\n- Charles Dickens published the novella A Christmas Carol in 1843.\n- A Christmas Carol is a 1938 American film adaptation of Charles Dickens's 1843 novella of the same name.\n- Reginald Owen starred in A Christmas Carol (1938) as Ebenezer Scrooge, an elderly miser who learns the error of his ways on Christmas Eve after visits from four spirits.",
